    {q:"Atoms of the same element with different numbers of neutrons are called ___.", options:["isotopes","molecules","compounds","ions"], answer:0},
    {q:"An atom that has gained or lost electrons and carries a charge is called an ___.", options:["ion","compound","isotope","element"], answer:0},
    {q:"Metals are generally found on the ___ side of the periodic table.", options:["bottom only","right","top only","left"], answer:3},
    {q:"Nonmetals are generally found on the ___ side of the periodic table.", options:["top only","left","center only","right"], answer:3},
    {q:"The number of electrons in the outermost shell of an atom are called ___ electrons.", options:["valence","core","inner","nuclear"], answer:0},
    {q:"Thomson plum pudding model proposed that atoms were made of electrons embedded in a ___.", options:["vacuum","negative cloud only","dense nucleus","positively charged mass"], answer:3},
    {q:"The modern periodic table arranges elements primarily by increasing ___.", options:["atomic number","melting point","atomic mass only","color"], answer:0},
    {q:"Elements called metalloids have properties that are ___.", options:["purely gaseous","identical to metals","intermediate between metals and nonmetals","identical to nonmetals"], answer:2},
    {q:"Dalton atomic theory proposed that all matter is composed of tiny, indivisible particles called ___.", options:["isotopes only","ions","atoms","molecules only"], answer:2}
